[16.308,"o","\r\n MADISON WISCONSIN 53706"]
[16.308,"o","\r\n"]
[16.8,"o","\r\n  POULTRY NUTRITION IN DISEASES AND IMMUNOLOGICAL RESPONSES"]
[16.8,"o","\r\n"]
[17.267,"o","\r\n                                                 GENERAL"]
[17.758,"o","\r\n              PRIMARY CLASSIFICATION         CLASSIFICATION"]
[17.758,"o","\r\n"]
[18.233,"o","\r\n        RPA   ACTVTY  CMMDTY  SCNCE   PRCNT    PRGM   JTC"]
[18.708,"o","\r\n        R311  A5000   C2900   F0910   100%     P4.03  J2C"]
[18.708,"o","\r\n"]
[19.208,"o","\r\n PRIMARY HEADINGS: R311 Biological Efficiency-Animals; A5000"]
[19.733,"o","\r\n Biological Efficiency of Plants, Animals; C2900 Poultry; F0910"]
[20,"o","\r\n Nutrition and Metabolism-Animal"]
[20,"o","\r\n"]
[20.458,"o","\r\n GENERAL HEADINGS: P4.03 Poultry; J2C Animal Production"]
[20.458,"o","\r\n"]
[20.925,"o","\r\n                     SPECIAL CLASSIFICATION AND HEADINGS"]
[21.45,"o","\r\n         XAHD   Animal Health and Disease Related          020%"]
[21.975,"o","\r\n         S2910   Egg Type Chickens                         100%"]
[21.975,"o","\r\n"]
[22.425,"o","\r\n      BASIC 050%    APPLIED 050%    DEVELOPMENTAL 000%"]
[22.425,"o","\r\n"]
[22.983,"o","\r\n  OBJECTIVES: To determine the requirement of copper for the immune"]
[23.533,"o","\r\n response  of the chick, andto determine measures of immunity that"]
[24.083,"o","\r\n are  affected  by copper deficiency. To characterize the clinical"]
[24.633,"o","\r\n signs  of  altered  copper  metabolism in chicks fed nutrients or"]
[25.075,"o","\r\n chemicals known to interfere with copper metabolism."]
[25.075,"o","\r\n"]
[25.633,"o","\r\n  APPROACH:  Day-old  chicks  will be fed a milk protein based diet"]
[26.183,"o","\r\n with  1,  2,  4, 6, 8, 10, or 20 mg/kg diet copper. Tissue copper"]
[26.733,"o","\r\n hematological  variables, enzyme activities, humoral and cellular"]
[27.283,"o","\r\n immunity,  and  macrophage function will be assessed. Chicks will"]
[27.833,"o","\r\n be  fed  adequate,  200, or 400 mg/kg copper factorially arranged"]
[28.383,"o","\r\n with  35 mg/kg diet thiram, 35 mg/kg diet Fusarochromanone, 1.45%"]
[28.933,"o","\r\n dl-methionine,  .005%  roxarsone,  or  a combination of 200 mg/kg"]
[29.483,"o","\r\n zinc plus .875% methionine plus .005% roxarsone, or 35 ppm thiram"]
[30.033,"o","\r\n plus 35 ppm Fusarochromanone. Measures of alter copper metabolism"]
[30.325,"o","\r\n will be measured as in approach 1."]
[30.325,"o","\r\n"]
[30.883,"o","\r\n  KEYWORDS:   COPPER  IMMUNITY  POULTRY  NUTRIENT-DISEASE-RELATIONS"]
[31.433,"o","\r\n IMMUNE-RESPONSE   CHICKS   NUTRIENT-DEFICIENCY  MINERAL-NUTRITION"]
[31.983,"o","\r\n METABOLISM  MILK-PROTEIN  DIET  ENZYME-ACTIVITY  HUMORAL-IMMUNITY"]
[32.392,"o","\r\n CELLULAR-IMMUNITY MACROPHAGES POULTRY-PRODUCTION"]
[32.392,"o","\r\n"]
[32.592,"o","\r\n  PROGRESS: 9201 TO 9212"]
[33.142,"o","\r\n A  number  of  Fusarium  species were shown to produce mycotoxins"]
[33.692,"o","\r\n capable  of  immune suppression. Copper was capable of preventing"]
[34.242,"o","\r\n the immune suppression and tibial dyschondroplasia (TD) induction"]
[34.792,"o","\r\n caused  by  fusarochromanone. A toxin produced by F. proliferatum"]
[35.342,"o","\r\n which induces neurological disorders in chickens was prevented or"]
[35.892,"o","\r\n reversed by thiamine injection or feeding. High levels of dietary"]
[36.442,"o","\r\n homocysteine and cysteine were shown to be inducers of TD. Copper"]
[36.992,"o","\r\n (150  ppm)  was effective in alleviating homocysteine-induced TD."]
[37.542,"o","\r\n Molybdenum  was  effective  in  preventing  cysteine-induced  TD."]
[38.092,"o","\r\n Copper  was also shown to prevent thiram- and antabuse-induced TD"]
[38.642,"o","\r\n and  copper.  Studies on the effects of copper and zinc on immune"]
[39.192,"o","\r\n function  showed  normal  responses  in  even  severely deficient"]
[39.742,"o","\r\n chicks.  High  zinc  was shown to depress tissue on copper levels"]
[40.292,"o","\r\n and induce anemia. The anemia was not easily corrected by feeding"]
[40.842,"o","\r\n high  levels  of  copper.  Apparently  high  use  of  these trace"]
[41.392,"o","\r\n elements interfered with iron absorption. Antibodies generated in"]
[41.942,"o","\r\n the hen by specific antigen injection which are passed to the egg"]
[42.492,"o","\r\n yolk  were  used successfully in routine immunological procedures"]
[42.792,"o","\r\n and to enhance growth of offpsring."]
[42.792,"o","\r\n"]
[42.917,"o","\r\n  PUBLICATIONS:"]
